      "message": "I really wish there were a better solution for `sk_sp` here. Note that there are open bugs about that rule contradicting other guidelines: https://www.mail-archive.com/llvm-bugs@lists.llvm.org/msg69102.html\n\nFor `sk_sp`, my take is that passing by value with `std::move` throughout would be even faster/better, followed by passing `const\u0026`, then passing by value. (The value is just a single pointer so it fits in a register ... passing by `const\u0026` essentially adds a level of indirection for no gain)?\n\nAlas, I don\u0027t think the clang-tidy rules are smart enough to be able to disambiguate... we could allow-list `sk_sp` (https://stackoverflow.com/a/70497291), but I think it would then let us get away with non-moved values? (Or maybe other rules would catch that mistake?)",
